<title>USA: Siskon sets $10.3 mln writedown on mine.</title>
<headline>Siskon sets $10.3 mln writedown on mine.</headline>
<dateline>GRASS VALLEY, Calif. 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siskon Gold Corp on Friday said it reduced the carrying value of its San Juan Mine by $10.3 million in the fourth quarter of 1996 because of higher-than-expected operating costs and a decline in gold prices.</p>
<p>&quot;Although the drop in gold prices is unfortunate, we feel it is best to take a writedown now and be poised to take advantage of any future upturn in prices,&quot; Siskon President Tim Callaway said in a statement.</p>
</text>
